# MarketHunter GIL Trading Scanner runtime - environment file example.
#
# Entirely optional: TRADING_SCANNER_DB_PATH already defaults to
# data/trading_scanner.db relative to WorkingDirectory= (the same
# default api/trading_scanner_api.py itself uses), so this file is
# only needed if the real deployment's scanner sqlite db lives
# somewhere else.
#
# If used, copy this to
# /home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/deploy/systemd/gil-trading-scanner-runtime.env
# (matching EnvironmentFile=-... in gil-trading-scanner-runtime.service -
# the leading "-" already makes a missing file harmless).
#
# There is no IBKR credential to set here yet -
# build_ibkr_universe_source() always returns None today
# (BLOCKED-IBKR-SESSION - see trading_scanner/universe.py). A future
# slice will introduce whatever env vars a real IBKR session boundary
# needs; none exist yet, so none are documented here.

#TRADING_SCANNER_DB_PATH=/home/ubuntu/MarketHunter/data/trading_scanner.db
